WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.268 --> 00:00:01.558
- Yeah, I was a good speller. Yeah.

00:00:01.558 --> 00:00:02.591
- Do you want to prove it right now?

00:00:02.591 --> 00:00:03.752
- Ohhh, Gosh!

00:00:03.752 --> 00:00:04.797
- Okay good because you don't have a choice.

00:00:04.797 --> 00:00:07.315
(upbeat music)

00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:11.299
- How are you at spelling?

00:00:11.559 --> 00:00:12.354
- At spelling?

00:00:12.354 --> 00:00:13.260
- (expletive) no!

00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.757
- I can not believe this is what this is.

00:00:14.757 --> 00:00:15.942
- If at any point, I'm here for you,

00:00:15.942 --> 00:00:16.881
if you need support...

00:00:16.881 --> 00:00:17.879
That's why I'm here.

00:00:17.879 --> 00:00:19.238
- It's fifth grade, you should be fine.

00:00:19.238 --> 00:00:20.980
- I said I was homeschooled
for God's sake.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:21.966
- So first word, here we go,

00:00:21.966 --> 00:00:22.663
spaghetti.

00:00:22.663 --> 00:00:24.845
- I usually call it pasta.

00:00:24.845 --> 00:00:26.865
- S-P-A...

00:00:26.865 --> 00:00:27.579
- G...

00:00:28.489 --> 00:00:30.338
- There's a secret H in there somewhere.

00:00:30.338 --> 00:00:32.083
- I don't know how to spell spaghetti!

00:00:32.083 --> 00:00:33.303
- E-T-I?

00:00:33.683 --> 00:00:35.177
- T-T-I, spaghetti.

00:00:35.177 --> 00:00:35.821
- That is correct.

00:00:35.821 --> 00:00:36.446
- Oh, yes!

00:00:36.446 --> 00:00:37.269
- Correct.
(groans)

00:00:37.269 --> 00:00:38.763
- That is correct, good job!

00:00:38.763 --> 00:00:39.613
- That is not correct.

00:00:39.613 --> 00:00:40.428
- I know.

00:00:40.428 --> 00:00:41.912
- When have I ever had to spell spaghetti?

00:00:41.912 --> 00:00:42.667
- Humiliated.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.162
(both laugh)

00:00:44.162 --> 00:00:44.803
Give it to me!

00:00:44.803 --> 00:00:45.604
- No. No.

00:00:45.604 --> 00:00:46.368
- Kids stay in school.

00:00:46.368 --> 00:00:47.704
Don't become actors.

00:00:47.704 --> 00:00:49.818
- Next word is diarrhea.

00:00:49.818 --> 00:00:51.170
- Ah, (expletive)!

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:52.992
Uh, uh, literally. Um...

00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:54.854
- You went right to it, you now this one.

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:57.314
- These are all like hidden H words.

00:00:57.314 --> 00:00:59.501
D-I-A...

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.621
- I hate this game.

00:01:01.621 --> 00:01:03.315
R-R-E-A-H?

00:01:03.315 --> 00:01:04.848
- I'm going to tell her
she's right no matter what.

00:01:04.848 --> 00:01:05.630
- I'm missing an R.

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:06.932
- Yeah, just throw it in there somewhere.

00:01:06.932 --> 00:01:08.791
- Die-uh-rhea

00:01:09.081 --> 00:01:10.677
- D-I-O-R-R-H-E-A?

00:01:11.107 --> 00:01:12.952
- So sorry, that is terrible diarrhea.

00:01:13.272 --> 00:01:14.235
- R-H-E-A?

00:01:14.235 --> 00:01:15.326
- Correct! Wow!

00:01:15.686 --> 00:01:16.636
- You know your diarrhea.

00:01:16.636 --> 00:01:17.932
- I know my diarrhea.

00:01:17.932 --> 00:01:19.823
- Last one might be the hardest,

00:01:19.823 --> 00:01:21.036
mediterranean.

00:01:21.036 --> 00:01:22.149
- Can we call a friend? (laughs)

00:01:22.569 --> 00:01:26.056
- M-E-D-I-T-T...

00:01:26.056 --> 00:01:27.407
- A-R...

00:01:27.407 --> 00:01:28.046
- R-

00:01:28.466 --> 00:01:29.091
- Oh!

00:01:29.971 --> 00:01:31.141
- How's that?
- [Interviewer] Smiley face.

00:01:31.141 --> 00:01:32.028
- Smiley face ending.

00:01:32.028 --> 00:01:32.948
- That was very wrong.

00:01:32.948 --> 00:01:35.783
(all sing) ♫ All that we
could do with this emotion ♫

00:01:35.783 --> 00:01:39.596
- M-E-D-I-T-E-R-R-E-A-N-E-A-N?

00:01:40.326 --> 00:01:41.769
- Correct!

00:01:41.769 --> 00:01:43.055
Correct! (celebrates)

00:01:43.055 --> 00:01:45.004
You're the first person
to spell mediterranean.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.653
- That is bad.

00:01:46.653 --> 00:01:47.861
- Well you know if I get any word wrong...

00:01:47.861 --> 00:01:49.278
I don't mind getting diarrhea wrong

00:01:49.278 --> 00:01:51.182
because maybe it's just
not an issue I have.

00:01:51.922 --> 00:01:52.502
Sooo...

00:01:52.502 --> 00:01:53.446
- The only one I do know how to spell.

00:01:53.446 --> 00:01:54.838
Do with that information what you will.

